1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,540
So on meetings, there's a requirement that the

2
00:00:02,540 --> 00:00:06,400
board meets quarterly to deliberate on the affairs

3
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:09,500
of the business and directors are expected to

4
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:12,020
attend at least two-thirds of those meetings

5
00:00:12,020 --> 00:00:14,260
to qualify for re-election.

6
00:00:15,960 --> 00:00:18,520
Directors are also expected to sit and serve

7
00:00:18,520 --> 00:00:21,500
on board committees and the codes and the

8
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:25,200
respective guidelines also define the kinds of committees

9
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:27,240
that the board should have.

10
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:30,120
I discussed conflicts of interest earlier on, this

11
00:00:30,120 --> 00:00:33,180
is also a code provision and the codes

12
00:00:33,180 --> 00:00:35,620
are required and the guidelines as well that

13
00:00:35,620 --> 00:00:38,780
directors should not just abstain from discussions but

14
00:00:38,780 --> 00:00:41,800
should also recuse themselves, meaning that they should

15
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:45,080
exit meetings where they have conflicts of interest.

16
00:00:45,980 --> 00:00:49,220
There's a requirement on auditors as well, of

17
00:00:49,220 --> 00:00:52,000
course, I mean each organisation will appoint auditors

18
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:54,920
but they are not supposed to serve for

19
00:00:54,920 --> 00:00:59,520
10 years consecutively after which they retire and

20
00:00:59,520 --> 00:01:01,600
then serve a pull-off period of five

21
00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:04,220
years following which they can be reappointed.

22
00:01:05,580 --> 00:01:07,680
There's a requirement also that the board should

23
00:01:07,680 --> 00:01:09,280
have a remuneration policy.

24
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:12,900
The remuneration policy should determine and define the

25
00:01:12,900 --> 00:01:16,360
kind of remuneration that directors are entitled to

26
00:01:16,360 --> 00:01:18,840
but this is strictly speaking restricted to seasonal

27
00:01:18,840 --> 00:01:22,320
allowance and directors fees as well as reimbursable

28
00:01:22,320 --> 00:01:26,240
expenses including travel and hotel expenses.

29
00:01:26,860 --> 00:01:29,580
To mention here that sometimes you find that

30
00:01:29,580 --> 00:01:31,480
directors earn other remuneration.

31
00:01:32,140 --> 00:01:34,940
Strictly speaking, this is not in consonance with

32
00:01:34,940 --> 00:01:37,780
the expectations of the code and the respective

33
00:01:37,780 --> 00:01:38,520
guidelines.

34
00:01:39,140 --> 00:01:42,140
Again, for the sake of emphasis, remuneration is

35
00:01:42,140 --> 00:01:45,200
limited or should be limited to directors fees,

36
00:01:45,580 --> 00:01:48,300
seasonal allowance and other reimbursable expenses.

37
00:01:48,520 --> 00:01:51,000
Of course, directors are also entitled to periodic

38
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:55,080
training which could be local training, could be

39
00:01:55,080 --> 00:01:58,400
international training but there should be a training

40
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:01,120
policy that allows directors to be exposed to

41
00:02:01,120 --> 00:02:04,320
periodic training and new directors are expected also

42
00:02:04,320 --> 00:02:07,979
to have an induction not just into the

43
00:02:07,979 --> 00:02:11,360
business of the company but also into the

44
00:02:11,360 --> 00:02:14,540
roles and responsibilities of the director.

45
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:17,720
Every company should have a company secretary and

46
00:02:17,720 --> 00:02:20,780
the responsibilities of the company secretary are clearly

47
00:02:20,780 --> 00:02:25,720
stated in the respective codes and guidelines but

48
00:02:25,720 --> 00:02:27,980
to just mention here that the office of

49
00:02:27,980 --> 00:02:31,180
the company secretary is rated almost as highly

50
00:02:31,180 --> 00:02:33,680
as that of a director by the respective

51
00:02:34,700 --> 00:02:36,280
codes and guidelines.

52
00:02:37,040 --> 00:02:39,040
The appointment of the company secretary is a

53
00:02:39,040 --> 00:02:41,840
board level appointment so is the removal of

54
00:02:41,840 --> 00:02:45,540
the company secretary so management cannot remove or

55
00:02:45,540 --> 00:02:49,040
appoint a company secretary without the authorisation of

56
00:02:49,040 --> 00:02:49,500
the board.

57
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:52,300
To also mention that the company secretary reports

58
00:02:52,300 --> 00:02:54,360
to the board and not to management.

59
00:02:54,580 --> 00:02:57,180
There's a dotted line reporting to the CEO

60
00:02:57,180 --> 00:02:59,160
or to the managing director by the company

61
00:02:59,160 --> 00:03:02,120
secretary but this is only related to administrative

62
00:03:02,120 --> 00:03:05,880
matters, functionally the company secretary reports or should

63
00:03:05,880 --> 00:03:08,860
report to the board through the board chair.
